 The presented view of status aligns itself with recent sociological approaches - which view power more generally as privileged access to opportunities for economic success (Kendall,
 exploitation in Tilly's view,
 Chancen in the Weberian framework) rather than a defertential hierarchy.
 While static social attributes do not sufficiently outline these views,
 the success-determining attributes are not circumsibed by social capital alone either.
 Following an approach similar to 
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout


\backslash
citeA{goode1978celebrationheroes}
\end_layout

