,
 we consider how social capital acts alongside with certain natural attributes to drive the success of an individual in competitions for objective status.
 These opportunities are represented as probability functions for promotion to a higher status position - that are in turn subject to social capital investments.
 In other words,
 the participants compete both with raw talent and acquired skills (social capital) to get promoted to (or to maintain) a 
