 the results of such a model have implications on how inequality shapes investment decisions made with a perception of mobility and how such concerns may aggregate into macroeconomic trends.
 Indeed a necessary feature of the above formulation is that the results help separate the subjective aspects of status (how expectation of the future affects individual decisions) from its objective aspects (i.e.
 the reality of income differences due to status).
 
\end_layout

