- the economic perspectives tend to contrast status as a social goal against the economic goals of a consumer.
 At least since Weber,
 a distinction is drawn between status and class - wherein status refers to fixed qualitative attributes such as race,
 regional identity,
 or gender,
 while class denotes one’s economic position 
\begin_inset ERT
